  "question": {
    "text": "\\(\\Delta_{\\text {vap }} \\mathrm{H}^{\\ominus}\\) for water is \\(+40.79 \\mathrm{~kJ} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\) at 1 bar and \\(100{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}\\). Change in internal energy for this vapourisation under same condition is \\(\\qquad\\) \\(\\mathrm{kJ} \\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\\). (Integer answer) (Given \\(\\mathrm{R}=8.3 \\mathrm{JK}^{-1} \\mathrm{~mol}^{-1}\\))",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "38",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\ell) \\rightleftharpoons \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}(\\mathrm{g}) \\quad \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\text {vap }}^0=40.79 \\mathrm{~kJ} / \\mathrm{mole} \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{H}_{\\text {vap }}^0=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {vap }}^0+\\Delta \\mathrm{n}_{\\mathrm{g}} \\mathrm{RT} \\\\ & 40.79=\\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {vap }}^0+\\frac{1 \\times 8.3 \\times 373.15}{1000} \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {vap }}^0=40.79-3.0971 \\\\ & =37.6929 \\\\ & \\Delta \\mathrm{U}_{\\text {vap }}^0 \\simeq 38\\end{aligned}$",
    "image": null
  },
